read `mentl audit main` serves, answered live from the session's one derivation. No arguments.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"teach","description":"Project each entry-file function's next annotation from the gradient — the one input that would unlock capabilities (an effect severance, a refinement, a representation pin). The same read `mentl teach main` serves, answered live. No arguments.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"frontier","description":"Project the entry file's whole ranked absence field from the resident graph — the oracle's frontier, the gradient's argmax uncollapsed. Every authored ?? hole first, each carrying its proven-survivor fan and tie-teaching; then the annotation-gradient positions. The same read `mentl main.mn:0` serves. Answer it, act on the head position, and ask again — the session re-derives as the tree moves. No arguments.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"map","description":"The read path by part — PLAN.md (the substance) and docs/SYNTAX.md (the surface) listed by heading and by PLAN §11's steps, each with its line and size; with a section, the one part it names by id (§11.2, S7.3), by title, or by a word it holds. The same read `mentl map [section]` serves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"section":{"type":"string"}}}}]}}
